{"compatibility":"minor","safety_note_md":"# SafeStan Safety Note

Compatibility: minor.

Protected data: `spin`.

Generated files: `model_safe.stan`, `data_safe.json`.

Changes: vectorized the observation of `spin` so the protected top-level data variable appears exactly once on the left side of a sampling statement. Added `spin_safestan_copy`, a deterministic copy of `spin`, to supply the neighbor values that the original model read while constructing the Bernoulli-logit predictors before scoring each element. In `data_safe.json`, `spin_safestan_copy[i] = spin[i]` for all `i`. Parameter priors were already explicit built-in distributions and were kept unchanged.
","model_safe_stan":"// ForestDB translation: Markov Logic Network
data {
  int<lower=1> N;
  array[N] int<lower=0, upper=1> spin;
  array[N] int<lower=0, upper=1> spin_safestan_copy;
}
parameters {
  real field;
  real coupling;
}
model {
  vector[N] eta;

  field ~ normal(0, 1);
  coupling ~ normal(0, 1);

  for (n in 1:N) {
    real neighbor_sum = 0;
    if (n > 1) {
      neighbor_sum += 2 * spin_safestan_copy[n - 1] - 1;
    }
    if (n < N) {
      neighbor_sum += 2 * spin_safestan_copy[n + 1] - 1;
    }
    eta[n] = field + coupling * neighbor_sum;
  }

  spin ~ bernoulli_logit(eta);
}
generated quantities {
  real aligned_pairs = 0;
  for (n in 2:N) {
    aligned_pairs += spin[n] == spin[n - 1];
  }
}
","data_safe_json":"{"N":4,"spin":[0,1,0,1],"spin_safestan_copy":[0,1,0,1]}","protected_variables":["spin"]}
